DeployIdentityConfirmLabelForkTest
├── when a sepolia candidate holds on chain
│   ├── it should publish the candidate's bytes under the label
│   ├── it should remove the candidate
│   └── it should return the recorded methods
├── when a mainnet candidate holds on chain
│   ├── it should publish the candidate's bytes under the label
│   ├── it should remove the candidate
│   └── it should return the zkPassport method and no Aadhaar method
├── when the candidate names another chain
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the recorded and the current chain id
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded zkPassport method has no code
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the address in the not deployed error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded Aadhaar method has no code
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the address in the not deployed error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded table differs from the table
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded role word differs from the live role
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should carry the recorded word and the live role
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded zkPassport method safe is not its safe
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the zkPassport method in the roles error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded Aadhaar method safe is the other methods safe
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the Aadhaar method in the roles error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the candidate swaps the two safes
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name a method in the roles error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the candidate swaps the two methods
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the Aadhaar method in the roles error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded codehash differs from the table
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the field in the record mismatch error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded version word differs from the table
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the field in the record mismatch error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded Aadhaar key differs from the table
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the field in the record mismatch error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when a mainnet candidate records an Aadhaar method
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the recorded address in the not deployed error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when an identity record shares its label stem with a core record
│   ├── it should publish the identity record under a name holding the dot
│   └── it should leave the core record untouched
├── when the recorded zkPassport method safe is zero
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should raise the zero safe error naming ZKPASSPORT_METHOD_SAFE
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded Aadhaar method safe is zero
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should raise the zero safe error naming AADHAAR_METHOD_SAFE
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when a mainnet candidate records an Aadhaar method safe
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the field in the record mismatch error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when a table address has lost its code
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name the address in the no code error
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the candidate carries an extra address key
│   ├── it should publish no key the checks did not read
│   └── it should publish exactly the nine record keys, each the checked value
├── when the candidate carries an extra unrelated field
│   ├── it should publish no key the checks did not read
│   └── it should publish exactly the nine record keys, each the checked value
├── when the recorded zkPassport method is a look alike
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name zkPassportMethod, the look-alike, the kit's code hash and the one found
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when a mainnet zkPassport method is a look alike
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name zkPassportMethod, the look-alike, the kit's code hash and the one found
│   └── it should publish no record
├── when the recorded Aadhaar method is a look alike
│   ├── it should revert
│   ├── it should name aadhaarMethod, the look-alike, the kit's code hash and the one found
│   └── it should publish no record
└── when the recorded Aadhaar method stores another verifier
    ├── it should revert
    ├── it should name aadhaarMethod, the method, the kit's code hash and the one found
    └── it should publish no record
